<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>An empty shipping box weighs 250 grams. The box is then filled with T-shirts. Each T-shirt weighs 132.5 grams.</para>
<para>The equation \( W = 250 + 132.5T \) represents the relationship between the quantities in this situation,
  where \( W \) is the weight, in grams, of the filled box and \( T \) is the number of shirts in the
  box.</para>
<!--Q1 -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Name two possible solutions to the equation \( W = 250 + 132.5T \).
      </para>
    </problem><solution>
    Enter your answer here:
  
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some examples:</para>
    <list>
      <item>\(T=2\) and \(W=515\)
      </item>
      <item>\(T=10\) and \(W=1575\)
      </item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Q2 -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What do the solutions mean in this situation? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    Enter your answer here:
  
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Each solution tells us the number of T-shirts in the box and the corresponding total weight in grams.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Q3 -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Consider the equation \( 2,\!900 = 250 + 132.50T \). In this situation, what does the solution to this
        equation
        tell us?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    Enter your answer here:
  
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>It tells us the number of T-shirts in the box that results in a total weight of 2,900 grams.</para>
  </solution></exercise></section>
</content>
